# MOVEMENT I — RECAPITULATION part 1: T1 (b161-176) and transition
# (b177-192).
# b161-168: T1 ff tutti as b17-24, but ostinato at L5 from the first bar
#   and a true perfect cadence (no deceptive turn this time).
# b169-176: LAYERS INVERTED: T1 sung by vc/cb/fg in the bass while both
#   violin sections hammer the CELL (L5 rhythm) above. The engine is on
#   top, the tune underneath.
# b177-192: the b33-48 transition re-routed to the dominant of G:
#   CELL16 imitation over g c f bb eb a(half-dim), then D pedal with G6/4
#   (B-natural: a glimpse of G MAJOR), ff with tp+timp (which could not
#   play on the F pedal in the exposition), collapse to pp.

